        "For three years, Mei had sat in the first chair of the school orchestra’s violin section. The first chair was the seat closest to the conductor, and the player who sat there led the other violins, played the solos and stood to shake hands with the conductor after every concert. Mei had practiced two hours a day to earn that seat, and she had never once thought about losing it.",
